<section class="section problem">
  <div class="container inner" data-reveal>
    <h2 class="h2">Raw CLI is the wrong abstraction for AI agents</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      RouterOS is powerful, but asking an LLM to improvise shell commands against production
      network gear is risky. MikroMCP gives agents a controlled tool surface: strict schemas,
      idempotent writes, dry-run previews, per-router circuit breakers, retry policies, RBAC,
      audit logs, snapshots, and rollback-aware change workflows.
    </p>
    <p class="accent mono">
      <span aria-hidden="true">›</span> MikroMCP turns MikroTik RouterOS into a production-minded MCP control plane.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .problem { text-align: center; }
  .inner { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .lede { margin: 22px auto 0; }
  .accent {
    margin: 30px auto 0; display: inline-block; font-size: 14px; color: var(--brand-glow);
    padding: 12px 20px; border: 1px solid rgba(20,184,166,.3); border-radius: 10px;
    background: rgba(20,184,166,.06); line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .accent span { color: var(--accent); margin-right: 6px; font-weight: 700; }
</style>
